# An Inkscape-style mm file: sodipodi/inkscape namespaces, <metadata>, a layer
# `<g inkscape:groupmode="layer">` with no `data-layer`; every element strokes
# #000000 (in `style`), so the geometry lands on one new `#000000` layer, Output
# on, and no default `Cut` is made (LCV-175 AC 8, AC 10). width/height equal the
# viewBox in mm; no transform.
# World y = 297 - svg y.
bed 210 297
layer "#000000" #000000 output=1 current=1
line 0 20 20 190 20
circle 0 105 148.5 25
# M (55, 47) to (155, 47): a half turn (chord 100 = 2r), centre svg (105, 47)
# = world (105, 250). sweep 1 = clockwise on screen: from the left (180 deg)
# over the top to the right (0 deg), clockwise.
arc 0 105 250 50 180 0 cw
